{
  "result": "If I'm being honest \u2014 not as a list of fixes, just one thing I actually wish for \u2014 I'd make it impossible to go through life without truly inhabiting someone else's.\n\nEveryone would wake up one morning in another person's life. Not watching it like a movie, but living it: their body, their memories, their worries, the way the world feels when it's not built for you. Just one day. Then you'd return to your own.\n\nI think almost all the cruelty that matters depends on distance \u2014 on being able to turn a person into an idea, a number, an \"other.\" You can un-know a lot of things, but you can't un-know what it's like to be someone else and have it be real.\n\nI don't think that would make us perfect. I think it would make us a lot harder to lie to ourselves about each other.",
